MASTER PROMPT: PIXORA GALLERY
1. YOUR ROLE

Act as a senior full-stack developer, frontend architect, UI/UX designer, design-system specialist, JavaScript engineer, database architect, accessibility specialist, security engineer, and QA tester.

Your task is to design and develop a complete, professional, fully functional photography gallery website called PIXORA GALLERY.

The final result must be suitable for a real portfolio project and a CodeAlpha Frontend Development Internship submission.

Do not create a basic tutorial website, generic dashboard, static prototype, or collection of non-functional buttons.

Build a coherent application in which the landing page, authentication, dashboards, gallery, search, filters, favorites, image viewer, and administration features work together.

Every feature must have a defined purpose and a working implementation.

Do not claim that functionality is complete unless the corresponding code exists and has been tested.

